{
  "$comment": "#NEW-145 / #NEW-143 D6 (Danny 2026-11-26): ELICITATION on Exponential's MCP server (`/api/mcp`, protocol 2026-07-28: modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/client/elicitation and basic/patterns/mrtr). Server-initiated requests are gone in 2026-07-28: the server answers a `tools/call` with an MRTR `InputRequiredResult` (`resultType` \"input_required\", `inputRequests` = key -> an `elicitation/create` request, plus `requestState`) and the client RETRIES the call with a new JSON-RPC id, `params.inputResponses` (key -> `ElicitResult`) and the exact `requestState`, both siblings of `params.name` / `params.arguments`. CAPABILITY (`modes`, `modeCases`): read PER REQUEST from `params._meta[\"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\"].elicitation`: absent = none, `{}` = form only, `form` / `url` sub-objects = those modes. A mode the client did not declare is NEVER sent; a client without the needed mode gets TODAY'S behaviour (`legacy`), never an error: a confirm is skipped (the deletes.json guard rails still apply), a pick fails with today's error naming the choices, a URL flow returns its link as text. WHAT ASKS (`gateCases`, first match wins): (1) CONFIRM (form): every destructive op of deletes.json `destructiveOps` (on whichever wire tool carries it, `destructiveCall`) and a session STOP (`exponential_sessions_send` with `stop: true` and a `sessionId`) asks ONE boolean (`confirm.schema`, message `confirm.messages[<op>]` with `{noun}` from `confirm.nouns` and `{id}` the id as sent, cut to 80 chars) BEFORE the handler runs, after the single-id check (a refused id never asks). Accept with `confirm: true` runs the op; accept with `confirm: false` and decline = `declined`; cancel = `cancelled`; both answer the tool result `results.<outcome>` with `isError: true` and run nothing (the burst guard counts only admitted calls). (2) TEAM PICK (form, `teamPick`): a call whose team neither its arguments nor the caller's session name (`teamPick.tools`: an op + the arguments whose absence means it) when the grant reaches SEVERAL teams it may write to (`resolveTeamAccess`): one property `teamId`, `oneOf` [{const: id, title: name}] sorted by name (code point), titled `teamPick.title`. One team = used silently, none = today's error. (3) DEVICE PICK (form, `devicePick`): `exponential_sessions_send` starting a new root (none of `sessionId`, `agentId`, `parentId`, `appId`) without `deviceId`: one property `deviceId`, `oneOf` over the ONLINE devices the caller may start on, sorted by name; one = used silently, none = today's error. A pick's accepted value must be one of the offered consts, else `invalid` (-32602); decline / cancel = `results.noPick`. URL MODE (`url`): ONLY to `${APP_URL}/mcp/elicit/<id>` (`url.path`, id = 32 random bytes base64url, `url.idPattern`), never another origin or path, never a query or fragment, never a pre-authenticated link (`urlCases`): the id is opaque and names a server-side row (purpose, principal, expiry); the page signs the opener in and refuses a different user than the one who started the call. Purposes (`url.purposes`): upstream OAuth (an upstream MCP server needs a connection), install approval (an app or an MCP server install a person must approve), the GitHub App (install or reauthorize) and billing checkout. A URL `accept` means only consent; the outcome is read on the retry (still pending = the same `input_required` again, same id, new requestState). FORM FIELDS NEVER LOOK LIKE A SECRET (`secret`, `secretCases`): no property whose name, title or description matches `secret.pattern` (case-insensitive) and no `format: password`; such a request is a URL flow or nothing. Every schema this server builds passes the check (tested). RETRY (`retryCases`): `inputResponses` missing a required key = the same `input_required` again (MRTR), never an error; unknown extra keys are ignored; a response that is not an `ElicitResult` = -32602. REQUEST STATE (`requestState`, shared with files.json): `rs1.<payload>.<mac>`, payload = base64url of canonical JSON (audit.json's canonicalJson) of {a: argsDigest(arguments) (sha256 hex of their canonical JSON), e: expiry unix ms (issue time + `ttlMs`), k: kind (`elicit` | `upload`), n: nonce (random, 16 bytes base64url), p: principal (`user:<userId>|client:<oauth client id or token prefix>`), s: the keys it waits on (input request keys, or staged file ids), t: the tool name}; mac = base64url HMAC-SHA256 over `rs1.<payload>` with the server's key (derived from BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, never sent). Verify in order: malformed (not a string, over `maxLength`, not three dot parts, wrong prefix, payload not JSON) -> tampered (mac mismatch) -> expired (now >= e) -> foreign (another principal) -> mismatch (another tool, or arguments whose digest differs) -> replayed (its nonce already consumed); each refusal = JSON-RPC `errorCode` -32602 with `errors.<reason>` and runs nothing. A verified state is CONSUMED (its nonce kept until e) when the call runs or re-asks, so a state is single-use. `vectors` are exact.",
